​
​[head=1]CONTRACT[/head]
​
​Between [bold]SCP-049[/bold] (hereinafter referred to as "The Plague Doctor") and the [bold]SCP Foundation[/bold] (hereinafter referred to as "The Foundation")
​
​[head=3]1. PURPOSE OF THE AGREEMENT[/head]
​This contract establishes the rules regarding the containment, interaction with, and limitations on the rights and obligations of The Plague Doctor and Foundation personnel. The document aims to ensure personnel safety, preserve the scientific utility of the object, and prevent the abuse of privileges by either party. 
​
​[head=3]2. PARTIES AND DEFINITIONS[/head]
​[bullet][bold]The Plague Doctor[/bold] — The object identified as SCP-049. 
​[bullet][bold]The Foundation[/bold] — The organization responsible for the containment, study, and control of SCP-049. 
​[bullet][bold]Foundation Personnel[/bold] — Employees of the facility who possess a keycard indicating their clearance level and whose legitimacy is recorded in the personnel registry console. 
​[bullet][bold]Emergency Situation (ES)[/bold] — An event posing an immediate threat to the lives and/or physical integrity of the facility and/or personnel (containment breach, armed engagement, etc.). 
​
​[head=3]3. GENERAL PROVISIONS[/head]
​[bullet]The Plague Doctor has signed this contract and thereby confirms his understanding of, and acceptance of, the terms contained herein. 
​[bullet]Signing this document does not render The Plague Doctor an employee in an organizational sense; SCP-049 remains a containment object with limited rights, as defined in this document. [bullet] The rights, privileges, and duties of the Plague Doctor are strictly limited to the provisions of this contract and the decisions of the facility's administration (the Facility Director, the Head of Research). 

[head=3]4. RIGHTS OF THE PLAGUE DOCTOR[/head]
[bullet] The Foundation undertakes to provide basic conditions of containment: security, sustenance, medical support, as well as the opportunity to conduct approved research sessions under staff supervision. 
[bullet] The Plague Doctor is permitted to make written and verbal statements to staff and researchers, provided such statements do not contradict the instructions of staff holding the appropriate clearance level (Facility Director, Head of Research, Head of Security). 
[bullet] Other privileges may be granted only with the express permission of the Head of Research or the Facility Director. 

[head=3]4.1. SPECIAL AUTHORIZATIONS FOR SCP-049 REQUESTS[/head]
[bold]Right to Request[/bold]
[bullet] SCP-049 has the right to submit requests for the provision of limited items and "patients" (Class D personnel), exclusively through personnel with Clearance Level 3 or higher. 

[bullet] Authorized items for medical procedures:
[bullet] Basic surgical instruments (scalpels, retractors, gloves, etc.); 
[bullet] Simple medical supplies (wound dressing kits, ointments, etc.) — strictly under the supervision of research staff or Security personnel; 
[bullet] Other items may be added to this list only with the written authorization of the Facility Director or the Head of Research. 

[bold]Patients (Class D)[/bold]
[bullet] SCP-049 has the right to request the provision of test subjects (Class D personnel) for the purpose of conducting "operations" or research. 
[bullet] The number of Class D personnel provided simultaneously shall be determined by the Facility Director and may not exceed the limit established by internal protocols. [bullet] All interactions between SCP-049 and D-Class personnel shall take place exclusively under the direct supervision of research staff or security personnel. 
​
​[bold]Restrictions and Conditions[/bold]
​[bullet] SCP-049 is not permitted to independently select specific D-Class personnel or objects. Such decisions shall be made by Foundation personnel, with the exception of items explicitly authorized under Section 4.1 of this agreement. 
​[bullet] Requests shall be processed in the ordinary course of operations and may be denied without explanation in the event of a security threat, an emergency, resource shortages, or at the discretion of facility administration. 
​[bullet] The provision of objects and test subjects is not a right inherent to SCP-049, but rather a privilege granted contingent upon his strict adherence to containment and safety protocols. 
​
​[bold]Abuse and Violations[/bold]
​[bullet] In the event that SCP-049 exhibits aggressive or manipulative behavior while submitting a request, he shall forfeit the privilege of submitting further requests for a period to be determined by the Site Director or the Head of Research. 
​[bullet] Any attempt to utilize provided objects or D-Class personnel outside the scope of an approved experiment shall result in immediate intervention by security personnel, the confiscation of said objects, and the application of containment countermeasures. 
​
​[head=3]5. RESTRICTIONS AND OBLIGATIONS OF THE PLAGUE DOCTOR[/head]
​[bullet] The Plague Doctor is not authorized to demand actions from Foundation personnel that contradict orders issued by the Site Director, the Head of Research, or security personnel. His statements do not carry the force of an official order. 
​[bullet] The Plague Doctor is obligated to refrain from any actions that pose a threat to the lives of Foundation personnel or the structural integrity of the facility.
[bullet] Manipulative, aggressive, or overtly demanding behavior on the part of the Plague Doctor is considered a violation of terms and will be subject to review.
